{
  "project_name": "codemonkey",
  "programming_languages": [
    "Python"
  ],
  "summary": "CodeMonkey is a scriptable, headless coding-agent CLI written in Python 3.11 (uv, Typer, Rich, httpx) that runs autonomous coding sessions against OpenAI-style and Anthropic-style endpoints \u2014 including a local llama.cpp server \u2014 using raw wire protocol with zero LLM SDKs. It provides one-shot and resumable exec runs, diff review, session management, execution-journal forensics, checkpoint/undo, an eval harness, and an interactive REPL, backed by 13 tools (shell, file read/write/edit, glob/search, repo_map, web_fetch, plan/memory updates, delegation) governed by rule-based permissions and approval policies. Reliability features include pre-write checkpoints, a verify gate with bounded corrective turns, idempotent mutating tools, auto-compaction strategies, prompt-prefix KV-cache stability, streaming wall-clock guards, observation budgeting with spill-to-disk, retry/backoff, and token/cost telemetry."
}
